A||N||2||RiceBurner515||Does a loose alternator belt prevent the battery from charging or starting?||||8||
Z||000000||RiceBurner515||11-22-2000||07:21 PM||||I have 2 quick questions:<P>1)Does a loose alternator belt prevent the battery from charging or starting?<P>2)Does a loose alternator belt cause hesitation or "sputtering" at low speeds? Or, could that just mean my cluth is slipping?||||reg||8
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-22-2000||07:30 PM||||1.  Yes.  A slipping belt doesn't allow the alternator to do its job properly, so it may not charge up the battery.<P>2.  I doubt it.  It could be a number of things, but I don't think a loose belt will cause hesitation.  Check the timing, plugs/wires, distributor cap/rotor, etc.  These items would cause hesitation if they are worn or fouled. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||11-22-2000||08:46 PM||||What you describe sounds as if all your problems are voltage related.If you tighten or replace your belt you may find all your problems are solved. ||||reg||1
